box(58,172,230,114,'HUMAN REVIEW','Analyst token; reviewed/dismissed status; no policy publication');arrow(352,229,290,229)
para('Separate optional analytics path: explicit user opt-in -> coarse allowlisted events -> configured PostHog transport. Failure never delays protection. Production requires authenticated reporters and a signed threat-update boundary.',58,117,1080,12,MUTED);finish()
base('ARCHITECTURE 02 / 03','Detection, data flow and intervention policy.','A deterministic rule-led cascade with bounded ML corroboration makes the decision reviewable.')
cards([('Input and feature contract','One event: channel, text or simulated payment, monotonic timestamp. Parse locally. Retain only tactic enums, model scores, derived coarse payment information and timing.'),('Workflow matching','Refund -> outgoing QR; authority + pressure -> transfer; guarantee -> escalating investment payment; fee-to-unlock; remote-control support; direct credential request. Ordered pretext checks prevent arbitrary keyword pooling.')],[('Gate and output','No risky action: quiet/watch. Matched action + sufficient independent signals: warning/high. Repeat suppress for 60s unless risk increases. Return reason, stage, evidence index, action-risk index and a user choice.'),('Fingerprint schema','version; random session_id; tactic set; ordered tactic sequence; channel set; amount_bucket; event_count. Maximum 64 events. Unknown fields, raw content and non-enum strings are rejected.')]);finish()
base('ARCHITECTURE 03 / 03','Review, escalation and operational safeguards.','No automatic blocking, threat-policy publication or fraud-account identification in the prototype.')
cards([('Candidate -> review','Distinct random session reports cluster by tactic and ordered-sequence similarity. Fixed 20/20 windows expose a shift cue under independence assumptions. Three reports create an unverified candidate. Analyst auth is required to mark reviewed or dismissed. A reviewed candidate is not proof of fraud.'),('User escalation path','Pause; contact the institution through independently sourced official details; export the redacted report. In a real suspected financial fraud, use official reporting channels. Automated external reporting is not implemented.')],[('Abuse and security','Sybil/poisoning threat is explicit. Rate limiting and deduplication are only baseline controls. Public rollout must add reporter trust, device/session attestation where appropriate, encrypted storage, auditability and red-team validation.'),('Privacy lifecycle','Raw input never enters API, analytics or cache. Fixed public app assets alone are cached offline. User-controlled report deletion; 24-hour server expiry. Granular consent; no SDK autocapture, replay or person profiles.')]);finish()
base('APPENDIX A / OPTIONAL','AI and asset disclosure.','All synthetic assets and models are labelled; no confidential customer or bank data is used.')
cards([('AI-generated content','ChatGPT/Codex generated code, documentation, visual design, SVG shield, synthetic text/scenarios and this PDF under user direction. Human review is required before contest submission.'),('Datasets and model','157 AI-authored training texts; 52 workflows (26 scam, 26 ordinary), including 32 later challenge fixtures. Two indirect scams are known misses. Eleven scikit-learn logistic heads; no ASR, deepfake or graph model ships.')],[('Third-party runtime and tools','Python/SQLite; browser APIs; bundled jsQR 1.4.0 (Apache-2.0); Node tests. scikit-learn 1.8.0 for training (BSD-3-Clause); ReportLab for PDF (BSD); Playwright for development checks; official GitHub actions. Optional PostHog capture API.'),('Visual and research assets','System font stacks in app; DejaVu fonts embedded in PDF; original generated SVG. No bank/company logos or stock imagery. Earlier pasted research statistics are not reproduced as independently verified results. All data/model artefacts are in the repository.')]);finish()
